@module briefing ; The briefing screen: the notes folder, the mission's text, the map
@about BriefingScreen $C98A is node $750E (zones BriefingZones $CA10). It copies the chosen mission's texts from the catalogue (CopyMissionText $70F6) to MissionData $DBF3, unpacks PicBriefing ($E949 of bank 7), adds three graphics and prints the briefing text at ($70A3). Its zones show the mission's map (ShowPauseOnce $7084: BriefingMapFrame $DACB and BriefingMap $DB64), print the title again ($709E) or go back.

$C98A c BriefingScreen ; The briefing: picture, three graphics, the mission text, then the zones with the map blit
$C9FB BriefingLoop
> The shadow screen, ShowBriefingMapOnce armed (`$7084` = 0), the Dragonfly's title hook `$6C56` = `RET`, the arrow pointer, SetBriefingBlit `$DBAA`, CopyMissionText, DrawBank7Picture `$E949`, BriefingBoxes, BriefingGraphicA-C, PrintString (`$70A3`), the map blit (`$83E6` = BlitMapView `$DBBD`), PointerZones until the view flag; then the 3D blit back (`$8999`) and NextView. Witness: L1 10 (menu).

$CA10 b BriefingZones 6 ; Zone table of the briefing
> `$709E` (BriefingTextOnce), ShowBriefingMapOnce `$7084` (the map), ScreenZero (back).

$CA23 c CopyMissionTextB6 ; CopyMissionText $70F6 called from bank 6
> Called by LoadMissionIfAllowed `$759A`. Witness: L1 15 (c1, death, m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$CA27 c CopyMissionTextOld ; Unused: an older copy of the mission's texts from the back buffer to $F9C4
> Known only from the code: nothing calls it. Once per mission (the operand `$CA2E`), from the catalogue's copy at `$8AF1`; sets `$70A3`, `$7D3C`, `$7D39`, `$7C55` and calls `$7D35`.

$CA86 b StoresTitleBox 5 ; The attribute box of the stores screen
> Read by StoresScreen `$CB1C`.

@module stores

$CA8B c StoresScreen ; The stores: picture, slots, the weapon and its turning model, until the mission starts
