@module results ; The end of a mission, the mission status card and the score
@about When a mission ends, the screen list runs MissionCompleteScreen $CD1E (node $755E) or MissionFailedScreen $CD84 (node $7564); both unpack PicCompletion ($E51E of bank 7). The completed one adds the mission's score ($68E2-$68E5) to Score $CC79, sets the mission's completion flag and prints the mission's own completion text (at $7C55); the failed one prints "MISSION FAILED." and the reason (at $7BF9). MissionStatusScreen $CDBF (node $756A) shows the commander's card with the missions completed and the score.

$CC54 c PrintFinalScore ; Unused: the mission's score as ten digits into $D461, then FinalScoreText
> Known only from the code: nothing calls it.

$CC6A c DotLeadingZeros ; Replace the leading "0" of the nine digits at $D49A with "[" (a full stop in SmallFont $7C59)
$CC6F BlankScoreLoop
> Witness: L1 4 (m10, menu, missions).

$CC79 b Score 4 ; The 32-bit score of the missions completed
> Added to by MissionCompleteScreen, set from a password by PasswordScreen, printed by PrintScore, coded by EncodePassword.

$CC7D c PrintScore ; Print the missions completed and the score (StatusText $D46C)
> LongToDigits `$D353` of Score into `$D49A`, DotLeadingZeros, PrintString `$D46C`. Witness: L1 4 (m10, menu, missions).

$CC93 b MissionsCompleted 1 ; The number of missions completed
> Counted by PasswordScreen and MissionCompleteScreen, printed through code 8 of StatusText.

$CC94 b FailedTexts 16 ; Texts: "MISSION FAILED." and the five reasons
> `$CC94` printed by MissionFailedScreen; the reason (the pointer `$7BF9`, set by the play code) is one of the five.
$CCAB UnitDestroyedText
$CCBE NoPickupText
$CCD8 DesertionText
$CCED OutOfFuelText
$CD01 BridgeText
@res texts/failed-texts.bin

$CD1E c MissionCompleteScreen ; Mission completed: PicCompletion, the score added, the flag set, the mission's text
> Sound off, DrawBank7Picture `$E51E`, Score += the mission's score, MissionsDone[mission] = `$FF`, PrintString (`$7C55`), SaveLoadedMission `$CD77`, the main screen, Delay, MissionsCompleted + 1, then the key wait of MissionFailedScreen (EndScreenKey). The completion recordings run it on page 6:
> Witness (not an L1 build of the json): m1complete frames 21560-21721, MissionsDone and Score written at 21590, 32 frames after HelicarrierHit; m4complete 21301-21462 (work/stage2/complete-NOTES.md).

$CD63 c Delay ; A delay of five times 65535 loops
$CD65 DelayOuter
$CD68 DelayInner
> Witness: L1 36 (c1, death, m10, m2erbe, m2ocean, menu, missions, play, play2, search).

$CD70 b EndZones 6 ; Zone table of the two mission end screens
> ScreenZero.

$CD77 c SaveLoadedMission ; Put LoadedMission's two bytes ($7E2C) into the mission's header ($70A3 +1 and +3)
> Witness: L1 13 (m2erbe, missions, play, play2).

$CD84 c MissionFailedScreen ; Mission failed: PicCompletion, "MISSION FAILED." and the reason, then a key
> Known only from the code: no recording runs it on page 6.
> Seen in work/stage2/rec/fuel (a POKE recording, never the image: Fuel `$7C57` = 32 at frame 7704): the failure reason `$7BF9` = `$ED` by frame 7904, MissionFailedScreen at frame 7862 shows PicCompletion with "MISSION FAILED." / "RAN OUT OF FUEL.", SaveLoadedMission `$CD77` at 7892, then the title (SetTitleWindow `$D10E`, the music from Bank4Start) at 8051: a failure ends at the title, there are no lives.
$CDA5 EndScreenKey
$CDA8 EndKeyLoop

$CDB5 b StatusBoxes 5 ; Two attribute box records of the mission status card
> Read by MissionStatusScreen `$CDE6` and `$CDEC`.
$CDBA StatusBoxB

$CDBF c MissionStatusScreen ; The mission status card: PicMissionStatus, two graphics, the score, then the zones
$CE00 StatusCardLoop
> DrawBank7Picture `$EC82`, StatusGraphicB (11 x 16), StatusGraphicA (10 x 32), the boxes, PrintScore, the pointer, PointerZones (StatusScreenZones) until the view flag, ShowWaitPointer, NextView. Witness: L1 4 (m10, menu, missions).

