@module font ; The 8x8 font of PrintString and PrintRawString
@about 98 glyphs for the characters $20-$81, 8 bytes each, the top row first. PrintChar ($6FF0, through GlyphAddress $6ED7) and PrintRawString $C6FC address glyph c at $F5E4 + 8 (c - $20). $80 and $81 are the map legend's road and river patterns. The small-font texts (code 7) use SmallFont $7C59 instead, where ":" is the space and "[" the full stop.

$F5E4 b Font8x8 8 ; The 8x8 font: characters $20-$81
> Read by PrintString's PrintChar (`$6EE1`) and by PrintRawString (`$C707`, `$C716`).
@res fonts/font8x8.bin

@module options ; The options screen: the choice of the control device
@about OptionsScreen $F8F4 is node $74F2 (from the title): it prints the five devices and waits for a key 1-5; the device goes to ControlDevice $67B6 (ReadControls $971A) and its line is shown in another colour.

